{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "Three pre-launch releases (0.6.266, 0.6.267, 0.6.268) that had no changelog entry anywhere are now recorded in the pre-launch archive, reconstructed from their own migration reports with dates bracketed by 0.6.265 and 0.7.0 rather than guessed.",
    "A new test requires every shipped migration report to have a changelog entry in one of the two changelogs. A newly cut release that forgets its CHANGELOG.md section now fails immediately instead of being discovered releases later.",
    "The 21 pre-launch versions whose release DATES exist only in the private development repository are enumerated in KNOWN_PRELAUNCH_CHANGELOG_GAP rather than backfilled with invented dates. The allowlist may only SHRINK, so each backfill must delete its own line and no new gap can be added to it.",
    "CHANGELOG.md's boundary sentence now names 0.6.268 rather than 0.6.265, and marks the maintainer archive it points at as internal -- docs/productization/ is not part of the public release export, so a published copy does not contain that file."
  ],
